        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Should I get a plain patio or a stamped one?",
            "answer": "<p>A broom finish costs less, hides wear better and is what most people choose. Stamped and decorative work costs more because of the color, stamping and sealing labour — worth it if the look matters to you. See our <a href=\"/pages/stamped-concrete-patios\">stamped patios</a> and <a href=\"/pages/decorative-concrete-patios\">decorative patios</a> pages.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does a patio take to pour?",
            "answer": "<p>Most residential patios are dug, formed and poured within a few days once we start, weather permitting. We give you the actual schedule with your quote.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will my patio crack?",
            "answer": "<p>Concrete moves, so we control where it cracks instead of pretending it won't — compacted base, reinforcement and control joints cut at the right spacing keep the slab looking like one clean surface.</p>"
          }
        }
